# Cursor rules for Prescription Explanation Tool

Project: Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, Vercel AI SDK 4 with OpenRouter, zod, vitest.
Source of truth: spec.md. Update its revision history when behaviour changes.

Security
- Secrets come from process.env in server code only (lib/env.ts). Never NEXT_PUBLIC_ for secrets.
- Never log, echo or hard-code API keys.
- Never log prescription text or chat content. Log counts, lengths, durations, error codes.

API code
- Validate input with zod schemas from lib/schema.ts before doing anything else (after the rate limit check).
- Return errors as { error: { code, message } } using lib/errors.ts. Codes look like AI-400, AI-401, AI-429, AI-500, AI-502, AI-503, AI-504.
- Use lib/logger.ts for logs (one JSON object per line).
- Route handlers that call the model set `export const maxDuration = 30`.

AI behaviour
- System prompt lives in lib/prompt.ts. Keep it scoped to explaining prescriptions.
- Tools expandSig and checkSafety wrap pure functions in lib/sig.ts and lib/safety.ts. Do not move logic into the route.

Style
- Functional React components, hooks, no class components.
- Tailwind utility classes; keep the UI readable and printable.
- Small pure functions with unit tests in tests/*.test.ts.
- Prefer clear names over comments; comment the why, not the what.

Before committing
- npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test
